1
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:13,040
January 1925

2
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:14,560
In a small town at the edge of the

3
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:15,360
frozen sea,

4
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:16,972
children are getting sick

5
00:00:17,122 --> 00:00:18,752
The only medicine that can save them is

6
00:00:18,752 --> 00:00:20,244
hundreds of miles away

7
00:00:20,394 --> 00:00:21,184
There are no roads

8
00:00:21,184 --> 00:00:22,584
The sea is frozen solid

9
00:00:22,584 --> 00:00:25,184
And flying in this cold is too dangerous

10
00:00:25,477 --> 00:00:27,347
So the town turns to the oldest way to

11
00:00:27,347 --> 00:00:28,547
travel in Alaska:

12
00:00:28,547 --> 00:00:29,492
dogs

13
00:00:29,642 --> 00:00:31,392
This is the true story of the race to

14
00:00:31,392 --> 00:00:32,832
save Nome

15
00:00:36,017 --> 00:00:37,967
Nome began as a gold rush town on the

16
00:00:37,967 --> 00:00:39,827
shore of the Bering Sea

17
00:00:39,977 --> 00:00:41,407
By 1925,

18
00:00:41,407 --> 00:00:43,995
about fourteen hundred people lived there

19
00:00:44,145 --> 00:00:44,695
Every winter,

20
00:00:44,695 --> 00:00:45,575
the sea froze,

21
00:00:45,575 --> 00:00:47,655
and the last ship of the year sailed away

22
00:00:47,655 --> 00:00:49,023
until spring

23
00:00:49,173 --> 00:00:49,843
From then on,

24
00:00:49,843 --> 00:00:51,563
the town was cut off from the world

25
00:00:51,563 --> 00:00:52,923
Mail came by dog sled,

26
00:00:52,923 --> 00:00:54,747
and the trip took weeks

27
00:00:54,897 --> 00:00:56,567
And there was only one doctor in town:

28
00:00:56,567 --> 00:00:58,007
Curtis Welch

29
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:02,393
In January,

30
00:01:02,393 --> 00:01:02,927
Dr

31
00:01:02,927 --> 00:01:05,062
Welch saw something that frightened him:

32
00:01:05,062 --> 00:01:06,182
diphtheria

33
00:01:06,871 --> 00:01:09,141
Diphtheria is a bacterial infection that can

34
00:01:09,141 --> 00:01:10,541
swell and block the throat

35
00:01:10,541 --> 00:01:13,095
It is especially deadly for children

36
00:01:13,245 --> 00:01:14,515
There was a medicine that worked,

37
00:01:14,515 --> 00:01:15,955
called antitoxin

38
00:01:16,682 --> 00:01:18,272
But Welch's supply had expired,

39
00:01:18,272 --> 00:01:20,232
and a new shipment would not arrive until

40
00:01:20,232 --> 00:01:21,339
spring

41
00:01:21,489 --> 00:01:21,839
Without it,

42
00:01:21,839 --> 00:01:23,479
the disease could spread through the whole

43
00:01:23,479 --> 00:01:23,799
town,

44
00:01:23,799 --> 00:01:26,199
and the villages around it

45
00:01:29,383 --> 00:01:31,453
Officials searched for antitoxin,

46
00:01:31,453 --> 00:01:33,727
and found a batch in Anchorage

47
00:01:33,877 --> 00:01:35,667
A train could carry it north to the end

48
00:01:35,667 --> 00:01:36,107
of the line,

49
00:01:36,107 --> 00:01:38,441
at a town called Nenana

50
00:01:38,591 --> 00:01:39,941
But from Nenana to Nome,

51
00:01:39,941 --> 00:01:42,701
there were still 674 miles of frozen

52
00:01:42,701 --> 00:01:43,821
wilderness

53
00:01:44,060 --> 00:01:45,570
Ships could not get through the ice

54
00:01:45,570 --> 00:01:48,130
The few planes in Alaska had open cockpits,

55
00:01:48,130 --> 00:01:50,530
and flying them in deep winter was judged too

56
00:01:50,530 --> 00:01:51,650
dangerous

57
00:01:51,955 --> 00:01:54,555
There was only one option left

58
00:01:57,717 --> 00:01:58,747
The plan was a relay,

59
00:01:58,747 --> 00:02:00,656
like passing a baton

60
00:02:00,806 --> 00:02:03,756
Twenty mushers and about 150 sled dogs would

61
00:02:03,756 --> 00:02:06,310
wait at stops along the mail trail

62
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:08,090
Each team would race its section,

63
00:02:08,090 --> 00:02:10,514
then hand the package to the next

64
00:02:10,664 --> 00:02:12,774
The serum was packed in a twenty-pound bundle,

65
00:02:12,774 --> 00:02:14,496
wrapped against the cold

66
00:02:14,646 --> 00:02:16,876
The mail usually needed weeks for this trail

67
00:02:16,876 --> 00:02:17,236
Dr

68
00:02:17,236 --> 00:02:19,396
Welch feared the serum would last only about

69
00:02:19,396 --> 00:02:21,996
six days in the brutal cold

70
00:02:25,183 --> 00:02:27,133
On the night of January 27th,

71
00:02:27,133 --> 00:02:28,253
the first musher,

72
00:02:28,253 --> 00:02:29,413
Wild Bill Shannon,

73
00:02:29,413 --> 00:02:31,361
set off from Nenana

74
00:02:31,511 --> 00:02:32,501
The cold was brutal,

75
00:02:32,501 --> 00:02:34,021
often far below zero,

76
00:02:34,021 --> 00:02:36,528
and the wind cut through fur and skin

77
00:02:36,678 --> 00:02:38,201
At roadhouses along the trail,

78
00:02:38,201 --> 00:02:40,788
mushers warmed the package by the stove before

79
00:02:40,788 --> 00:02:42,287
heading out again

80
00:02:42,437 --> 00:02:43,307
Team after team,

81
00:02:43,307 --> 00:02:44,667
the serum moved west,

82
00:02:44,667 --> 00:02:45,427
through forests,

83
00:02:45,427 --> 00:02:48,027
along frozen rivers and across open tundra

84
00:02:48,811 --> 00:02:49,241
Meanwhile,

85
00:02:49,241 --> 00:02:51,841
the most famous musher in Alaska was racing to

86
00:02:51,841 --> 00:02:53,281
meet it

87
00:02:56,350 --> 00:02:58,180
His name was Leonhard Seppala,

88
00:02:58,180 --> 00:03:00,496
a champion sled dog racer

89
00:03:00,646 --> 00:03:02,036
His lead dog was Togo,

90
00:03:02,036 --> 00:03:04,796
a small husky who was already twelve years old,

91
00:03:04,796 --> 00:03:06,685
old for a sled dog

92
00:03:06,835 --> 00:03:07,985
But Togo was fast,

93
00:03:07,985 --> 00:03:08,465
smart,

94
00:03:08,465 --> 00:03:09,905
and fearless

95
00:03:10,121 --> 00:03:12,351
Seppala's team set out from the Nome side,

96
00:03:12,351 --> 00:03:14,755
heading east to meet the serum halfway

97
00:03:14,905 --> 00:03:15,655
To save time,

98
00:03:15,655 --> 00:03:17,895
they would have to take a shortcut most mushers

99
00:03:17,895 --> 00:03:19,655
would never dare

100
00:03:22,850 --> 00:03:25,000
The shortcut went straight across Norton Sound,

101
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,600
a huge bay of frozen sea ice

102
00:03:27,936 --> 00:03:29,766
The ice could crack and break apart at any

103
00:03:29,766 --> 00:03:30,086
moment,

104
00:03:30,086 --> 00:03:31,926
and drift out to sea with a team on

105
00:03:31,926 --> 00:03:32,755
it

106
00:03:32,905 --> 00:03:34,349
In darkness and howling wind,

107
00:03:34,349 --> 00:03:36,175
Togo led the team across,

108
00:03:36,175 --> 00:03:38,340
keeping them on solid ice

109
00:03:38,490 --> 00:03:39,000
They made it,

110
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:39,840
met the serum,

111
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:42,440
and crossed the ice again on the way back

112
00:03:42,717 --> 00:03:44,307
It was one of the most dangerous parts of

113
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:46,067
the whole journey

114
00:03:49,350 --> 00:03:51,380
Most teams in the relay ran around thirty

115
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:52,401
miles

116
00:03:52,551 --> 00:03:56,141
Seppala and Togo covered about 264 miles in

117
00:03:56,141 --> 00:03:56,661
total,

118
00:03:56,661 --> 00:03:58,648
more than any other team

119
00:03:58,798 --> 00:04:00,588
They carried the serum across the longest and

120
00:04:00,588 --> 00:04:02,526
toughest stretch of the route

121
00:04:02,676 --> 00:04:03,546
Then they handed it on

122
00:04:03,546 --> 00:04:06,026
The final legs belonged to two other mushers:

123
00:04:06,026 --> 00:04:08,426
Charlie Olson and Gunnar Kaasen

124
00:04:08,784 --> 00:04:10,654
And Kaasen's lead dog was about to become

125
00:04:10,654 --> 00:04:11,008
famous:

126
00:04:11,008 --> 00:04:12,128
Balto

127
00:04:16,017 --> 00:04:17,367
Kaasen set out at night,

128
00:04:17,367 --> 00:04:19,629
straight into a terrible blizzard

129
00:04:19,779 --> 00:04:21,529
The snow was so thick he could barely see

130
00:04:21,529 --> 00:04:23,426
the dogs in front of him

131
00:04:23,576 --> 00:04:25,606
But Balto kept the team on the trail,

132
00:04:25,606 --> 00:04:27,792
finding the way through the storm

133
00:04:27,942 --> 00:04:28,572
At one point,

134
00:04:28,572 --> 00:04:31,172
a gust of wind flipped the sled over

135
00:04:31,449 --> 00:04:32,919
The precious package was gone,

136
00:04:32,919 --> 00:04:34,999
somewhere in the snow

137
00:04:38,483 --> 00:04:40,473
Kaasen took off his mittens and searched the

138
00:04:40,473 --> 00:04:42,513
snow with his bare hands

139
00:04:42,663 --> 00:04:43,093
Finally,

140
00:04:43,093 --> 00:04:44,386
his fingers touched the bundle

141
00:04:44,386 --> 00:04:46,244
The serum was safe

142
00:04:46,394 --> 00:04:47,504
At the next relay stop,

143
00:04:47,504 --> 00:04:49,948
the fresh team was not ready to go

144
00:04:50,098 --> 00:04:51,088
Rather than lose time,

145
00:04:51,088 --> 00:04:53,688
Kaasen decided to keep going himself

146
00:04:54,034 --> 00:04:56,634
Nome was only about twenty miles away

147
00:05:00,383 --> 00:05:02,773
At about 5:30 in the morning on February 2nd,

148
00:05:02,773 --> 00:05:05,373
Kaasen and Balto pulled into Nome

149
00:05:05,980 --> 00:05:07,890
The relay had taken just five and a half

150
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:08,250
days,

151
00:05:08,250 --> 00:05:10,195
a record for that trail

152
00:05:10,345 --> 00:05:10,695
Dr

153
00:05:10,695 --> 00:05:13,295
Welch began giving the antitoxin right away

154
00:05:14,166 --> 00:05:16,036
More serum followed in a second relay,

155
00:05:16,036 --> 00:05:18,116
and within weeks the epidemic was under

156
00:05:18,116 --> 00:05:19,236
control

157
00:05:19,425 --> 00:05:21,615
The town had been saved by twenty mushers and

158
00:05:21,615 --> 00:05:23,055
their dogs

159
00:05:26,517 --> 00:05:27,827
Balto became a celebrity

160
00:05:27,827 --> 00:05:29,947
In December 1925,

161
00:05:29,947 --> 00:05:32,267
a statue of him was unveiled in New York's

162
00:05:32,267 --> 00:05:33,027
Central Park,

163
00:05:33,027 --> 00:05:35,539
with Balto himself there to see it

164
00:05:35,689 --> 00:05:37,399
Many mushers felt that Togo,

165
00:05:37,399 --> 00:05:39,639
who ran the longest and most dangerous stretch,

166
00:05:39,639 --> 00:05:41,380
deserved more credit

167
00:05:41,530 --> 00:05:41,960
Today,

168
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:44,200
historians agree that every team was part of

169
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:45,409
the rescue

170
00:05:45,559 --> 00:05:46,309
And every March,

171
00:05:46,309 --> 00:05:49,149
the Iditarod sled dog race follows parts of the

172
00:05:49,149 --> 00:05:49,829
old trail,

173
00:05:49,829 --> 00:05:52,429
in memory of the race to save Nome

174
00:05:53,150 --> 00:05:53,940
Twenty mushers

175
00:05:53,940 --> 00:05:55,420
About 150 dogs

176
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:56,540
One small package,

177
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:59,050
carried through the coldest place in America

178
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:00,862
Who do you think deserves the most credit:

179
00:06:00,862 --> 00:06:01,566
Balto,

180
00:06:01,566 --> 00:06:02,270
Togo,

181
00:06:02,270 --> 00:06:03,776
or the mushers?

182
00:06:03,926 --> 00:06:05,380
Tell me in the comments

183
00:06:05,530 --> 00:06:08,130
Subscribe so you don't miss the next episode
